//<[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]] turns off the television. He and [[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]] are sat in [[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]'s apartment in New York City, United States of America.>//



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** Quite unusual response from Carter. I wonder what is going on behind the facade.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Isn't that your assigned function to figure such out?



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** You try figuring out up and down in the middle of a global crisis.



//<[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]] sighs, the sound she emits crackles with electricity.>//



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** I'm not sure how to handle Brazil, truth be told. It's quite obvious that the Insurgency is doing their best to obscure their movements, and I don't even want to know what MC&D are doing. Not to mention whatever undiscovered anomalous organizations are hiding in the Amazon are doing about the pillar.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Our old Roman friend sure knew how to make many of his pillars painfully inaccessible to us. 3 out of 5 pillars require us to sweat for them. 



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** The world order was different back then, I suppose. Let's tally, though. We have MC&D's word that they'll guard Antarctica for us for roughly 5 million dollars worth of pure gold. Good thing our operatives down in Antarctica found someone so hungry for gold that they'd spin a few words to their superiors. I do suppose they're stockpiling resources for a potential collapse of the dollar, so perhaps that's why that worked.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** That'd be absurd.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** Right. Then we have India which...



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Thoroughly handled.



...



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** That'd be the sane assumption, yes.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Then we have Rome, which also seems to be collapsing into conflict. They-- really value those pillars, there. Must be religious in nature?



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** That leaves Brazil and Senegal. Both appears to be outside direct Foundation control.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** ... So only the Indian pillar is under our control.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** Assuming MC&D allows us to take over Antarctica as they promised, potentially 2 pillars are under our direct control.



//<[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]] twitches an eye. A lens is replaced as she blinks.>//



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** We're... not as prepared as I was led to believe to handle these scenarioes. World has changed faster than we have, I suppose.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** The other GoIs are familiar with us, it's hard to use the shadows when they know to bring flashlights at this point.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** And who do we have to blame for that, mh?



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** ...



//<The television turns on once more, revealing [[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]] in Antarctica with the pillar in the background. Prof. von Leisere seems to be pacing around the pillar in the background.>//



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** I see you're making full use of my charity.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** The satin sheets are to die for.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** How goes Antarctica?



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** Curiously. I've commandeered your two operatives and sent them to Senegal, given Four's-- misadventures. The curse specialist I've brought, the eccentric one from Site-03, is currently investigating something troubling.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** What, eye contact?



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** Not quite. The pillar responds to verbal phrases, and seems to be responding to a Latin incantation.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Did you just start randomly citing Latin near the big, ominous obelisk of anti-magic?



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** No, but a researcher did read the phrase carved into the pillar out loud. A few phrases seemed to activate thaumaturgic energy in the anomaly.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** And the effect of this incantation?



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** Unclear. And I don't exactly want to figure it out due to the scale that SCP-9070 came onto centerstage with.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** What does the thaumaturge behind you suppose?



<[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]] glances over her shoulder and looks into the camera with an apologetic smile.>



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** I quote: //"I deal with curses, not generalized thaumaturgy, how should I know?"//



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** And the rest of the thaumat--



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Containment efforts.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** Ah, those again! At which point do we let a few boogeymen go wild so we can get this situation handled? Let the GOC deal with it.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** The GOC are fully focused on the pillars. And we both know the clean-up would be unacceptable.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** So would the loss of the entire anomalous research we've been doing for a century or two.



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** I'll secure Four and haul him here. He's acquainted with traditional thaumaturgy.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** Right. Six and I will depart for Rome so we can get a first-hand account of what that whole crumbling sand castle is up to, given we cannot afford to send some operatives there "due to safety concerns" after a never-happened-before event.



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Cut your whining. The only reason why we know it to have never happened before is due to dealing with things using the scientific method, Five. Not by rushing in.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** I'm starting to understand why Eleven is such a childish rebel with this antiquated council.



**[[span class="o5 o5-10" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-10[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Summoner[[/span]][[/span]]:** Look, if you're going to fight, please do so outside my property investments? I'd hate to have the interi--



//<[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]] turns the television off and stands up.>//



**[[span class="o5 o5-6" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-6[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Singularity[[/span]][[/span]]:** Alright, let's get going.



**[[span class="o5 o5-5" tabindex="0"]][[span class="main"]]O5-5[[/span]][[span class="alt"]]The Shadow[[/span]][[/span]]:** As you say.



**<END LOG>**



[[/div]]



-----



[[=]]

++ **Addendum 9070-3-6:** Excerpt on the use of thaumaturgy in combat

[[/=]]



[[div class="almendra-regular" style="background-color: #1A0500; text-shadow: 2px 2px 2px #000000; color: #B4979F;border-color: #C2847A; border-style: groove; border-width: 5px; padding:15px"]]

[[=]]

[[span style="font-size: 40px"]]**Basic Evocation in Combat**[[/span]]

[[span style="font-size: 20px; margin-top 2px"]]//by Professor Weii, Serpent's Hand Evocation & Peacekeeping Expert//[[/span]]

[[/=]]



There's one thing you must understand about magecraft in conflict. If your magic cannot match or deflect a gun, you are not ready to use magecraft in conflict. It is that simple.



I will not be hearing about niche advantages. It's called The Great Equalizer for a good reason. Sure, it can be used to lend aid in combat, but guess what? Then you're most likely holding a weapon -- weakening your spellcraft.



Before you bring it up, yes, there are traditional spellblades who've weaved between martial prowess and magic. No, you're not one of them if you're reading this. There are two variations of magecraft that dictate the LOWEST barrier of entry. Shield and bolt. Or projectile. Or blast. Call it whatever you wish, you may be a talented thaumaturge under a strict categorization of spells, or you might use wild magic that's more explosive but less adaptable.



It matters little what background of magic you have and it matters a lot more what you put in front of you. Let's understand the thing that will keep you alive long enough to master the other, shielding.



Back in the "good old days", I'm told that you were simply required to shield a specific incoming attack or barrage. Well, guess what, every attack nowadays is a barrage. A single weapon may unleash a barrage on itself.



So, shields are important. Have you ever noticed why we don't have that many insufferable elder wizards around? A good bit of them are hiding from or are dead to gunfire. There are texts that describe many a woe made by magical societies about an apocalypse of steel and gunpowder that'd wipe us all out of existence. They were, admittedly, almost right. 



Luckily they spent a few decades to a century trying to figure out how to halt these firearms. However, they were always a little slower than the Mortal Empires in their research. This has started to turn in modern times. We have, at least I hope, some of the peaks of assault rifles in circulation now. So we're more than caught up ever since a thesis released in 2015 by Weißenwrachz. My thesis.



I know you're reading this, wanker. I know where you live.



Now one can partake in a very elegant, specific ritual that has been mastered by the most talented abjurers. It allows skilled magi to funnel small portions of energy into it at a consistent rate, so you needn't react to gunfire, a feat rather difficult even in these times. It works like a battery though, and it can run out-- in this case you either run or funnel a significant portion of energy into your chosen focus. That's how you stay alive with AK-47s and all his siblings.



Next is offensive magic. If you've skipped to this point without reading the defensive part, congratulations. The hypnotic signature that the last part of the last paragraph dispels has now made you afraid of the color blue for the next week. Good luck!



In order to cast effective magic in combat, you need to be reminded of a pretty base fact regarding spellcrafting. Not because I don't trust you, I just don't think you can do it properly. The more advanced, that is, the more properties your attempted spell has, the more energy you need to expel. You see how that goes in the same scale as the defensive tangent I was on earlier?



Don't. Waste. Energy.



I know that the ancient depicts wonderful styles of magic that allowed us to do so much more, and I'm sure there are some alive who actually had the pleasure to experience that. I'm sorry you cannot do this anymore. Use the magic you need to and get out.



No tricks. No fancy moves. Do not put yourself in danger.



Now, let's discuss specific spellcraft, the first thing you want to do is [[span style="font-family: Consolas,monaco,monospace;"]]**[REDACTED AS PER THE DANGEROUS MAGIC AND MAGICIANS ACT OF 2001]**.[[/span]]



[...]



Now remember, if with magic you cannot befell 'em, rely on the good old Parabellum.



[[/div]]



-----



[[=]]

++ **Addendum 9070-3-7:** Dr. Wrenna's arrival to Dakar, Senegal.

[[/=]]



[[=]]

+++* 6 DAYS, 10 HOURS AND 10 MINUTES AFTER SCP-9070

[[/=]]



Sgt. Vestergaard's location continues to be unknown, it is presumed that he has regenerated and moved to shore, or is in the progress of doing such. Due to lack of available personnel after SCP-9070, Afrastella Maskmaker and Tarel'ka the Gilded were tasked with assisting Dr. Wrenna on the condition that they did not reveal themselves to be anomalous to overveil individuals.



-----



[[div style="border:solid 3px; padding:15px; margin-bottom: 10px;"]]



[[=image Dakar%20Roofs%20-%20Beach%20%26%20Ocean.jpg size="medium" style="border-style: simple; border-width: 3px; border-color: #c1c1c1"]]



[[div style="margin-top: -20px"]]

[[=]]

^^//Dakar, Senegal as seen from above.//^^

[[/=]]

[[/div]]



**<BEGIN LOG>**



//<Afrastella Maskmaker, Tarel'ka the Gilded and Dr. Wrenna are standing on the ocean outside Dakar. Both Afrastella Maskmaker and Tarel'ka the Gilded have disguised themselves to be human. Afrastella Maskmaker has taken on the form of a woman in a long summer dress with jewelry of occult association as a necklace, rings and armbands. Tarel'ka the Gilded is wearing a black, striped suit with a white shirt and a green tie. He has a wide brim fedora with a green band around it.>//



**Dr. Wrenna:** Are you sure they-- can't see us?



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]I am in a shape where I can use magic, yes. Disguises and actionability in disguises are our strengths.[[/span]]



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]RUNNING TO THEIR LITTLE SKY-HOVELS ARE TOO, RIGHT? FOR SOME REASON, WHENEVER I SEE ONE OF YOU, IT'S ALWAYS WHEN YOU'RE SPRINTING AWAY FROM ME.[[/span]]



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]Or perhaps we'd like to maintain our ability to hear when yo--[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** I get it, okay? Can we-- can we just focus? We need a //plan//, here.



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]YOU DIDN'T SPEND THE TRIP HERE FORMULATING A PLAN?[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** Look, Thorstein usually does that when we're in the field. You can't just-- you--, well expect me to do that on the spot.



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]Ah, reliance upon allies is usually many a warlord's downfall.[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** Let me-- let me think.



//<Afrastella Maskmaker and Tarel'ka the Gilded exchange a glare. Afrastella Maskmaker squints her eyes while Tarel'ka the Gilded bares his teeth. 11 seconds passes.>//



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]WELL?[[/span]]



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]Plans don't form from impatience, brute.[[/span]]



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]AND ACTION DOESN'T FORM FROM OVERTHINKING. THAT'S WHY YOU LITTLE SNIVELING LIZA-[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** That's it.



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]WHAT?[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** We can't form a plan because we do not have the //information//. The plan is to gather information.



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]There we are. How do you desire to go about that?[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** You can be invisible, right?



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]It is so. I can also disguise myself to a variety of creations, unlike the manchild there.[[/span]]



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]DON'T NEED SHAPES OTHER THAN COINS.[[/span]]



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]... Those ar--[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** Afrastella, I need you to move above the city and use your senses there. I need to know where there are hotspots of thaumaturgy, this way we can pinpoint potential hideouts from the various factions here.



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]As you wish.[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** Gilded, need you on the ground in the bars. Chat people up, ask about what's going on in the city. Pay attention to any strange deaths, local legends and odd individuals.



**Tarel'ka the Gilded:** [[span class="demonG"]]DRINK, TALK AND LISTEN? VERY WELL.[[/span]]



**Dr. Wrenna:** We'll meet--



//<Dr. Wrenna points to an area outside the city.>//



**Dr. Wrenna:** There. By the coast come dawn.



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]Ah, from dusk 'til dawn. My favorite time. What of yourself?[[/span]]



//<Dr. Wrenna squints his eyes.>//



**Dr. Wrenna:** I think that... I'm going to go back to my roots.



**Afrastella Maskmaker:** [[span class="demonB"]]So be it. We shall meet soon.[[/span]]



//<Afrastella Maskmaker levitates into the air and accelerates towards the center of Dakar. She fades from view after flying 10 meters away. Tarel'ka the Gilded places both of his hands in his trousers' pockets and walks off towards the city while humming. Dr. Wrenna eyes the turist trap internet café in the distance and sighs.>//



**<END LOG>**



[[/div]]



-----



