[[div class="genbox highlight" style="margin-left: var(--docHighlightMargin);"]]

The parking lot is expansive and in abnormally good repair. There are a few cracks, of course, but nothing to suggest the profound disuse the place doubtlessly suffers from.



The lot itself is abandoned, but the surrounding area isn't. There are many businesses (and many cars) around the place, it is only the lot itself that's empty. I must wonder if this is due to an antimemetic effect (I have taken additional mnestics in preparation of this eventuality) or if it is simply an urban myth that keeps people away. This place surely has picked up a couple rumors over the decades, after all.



[[/div]]



@@@@

@@@@

[[div class="genbox highlight"]]

There are no signs of any anomalies yet, but something is off. I get the distinct feeling that I am being watched. Additionally, I parked near a streetlight and heard quite the racket coming from it. I broke open the plastic shell around the internals with my car-jack. Inside, I saw many many gears, churning noisily (I am grateful this place is abandoned, or a civilian would certainly have heard them at some point). I cannot guess as to what purpose the mass of machinery could possibly serve, but I am certain it is not to power a streetlight. Of note, once they were revealed, the gears powered down and came to a still. I doubt they were truly reacting to //me//, though I admit I found it disconcerting.

[[/div]]





[[/tab]]



[[tab Fence]]



[[div class="addendum" style="float: var(--image-float); margin: 1rem; width: 60%;"]]

[[image gate.png style="animation: blur-in 1s;"]]

[[/div]]

[[div class="genbox highlight" style="margin-left: var(--docHighlightMargin);"]]

The fence, if that's what you choose to call it, has become rather ineffective at keeping people out. It is tattered with holes. This is clearly not the first time it has fallen into disrepair. At some point the old fence became too damaged (it is a simple, short thing with limited barbed wire, perhaps security needs simply increased), and they replaced it with the second fence. This too has become damaged with time.



I did a brief perimeter sweep to see if I could find any easy entrances to the compound, and from there a side entrance to the facility proper (I suspect walking in the main door would be a terrible decision). I was presented with a great number of choices to make my entrance, the fence is ravaged. People may not come here, but animals certainly do. That said, I have not heard any birdsongs or other signs of life since I arrived.

[[/div]]



@@@@

@@@@

[[div class="genbox highlight"]]

A few things of note. One: I am over 3 kilometers from my car. The path from the parking lot to the facility was disturbingly long. I monitored for signs of non-Euclidean geometry but came up blank. That said, I am certain the original opera house would not have been built this way. Even if the geometry is now stable, something must have altered it. The surrounding forest of the path is clearly ancient, however, so surely the facility was not moved recently. 



Two: I did find a single sign, the only writing in the surrounding area. It was unique and heavily damaged. It read: '**Keep Out. Nothing you can do here is as important as returning home. People love you. If you enter these premises your life and soul are forfeit. No known religion is capable of protecting you from what's within. You are not exempt from suffering.**

