[[tabview]]



[[tab Mudroom]]



[[div class="addendum" style="float: var(--image-float); margin: 1rem; width: 60%;"]]

[[image mudroom.png style="animation: blur-in 1s;"]]

[[/div]]

[[div class="genbox highlight" style="margin-left: var(--docHighlightMargin);"]]

I have entered the facility. I don't really know what to call the place I'm in now. I'm going with 'mudroom', since it has benches and coat racks and closets, though 'entrance hall' could work just as well. I have, accordingly, taken off my coat and my muddy boots. I see my error, of course, it is entirely possible that I will be leaving in a rush, through some other entrance, and therefore not be able to recover my items. That said, when entering places like this I find it better to follow the customs, as breaking from them often results in far worse things than a lost coat (and a subsequent trip to REI).



What's strange is that the lights are still on, and the place is by and large clean. I'd do the car-jack trick again on the walls but I don't want to make too much noise. I have no way of knowing if I'm truly alone, and, judging by the sign outside, I'm not.

[[/div]]



@@@@

@@@@

[[div class="genbox highlight"]]

I am now faced with the opportunity of going up, or down, knowing full well that I will probably not be able to return here, if prior experience is anything to go by. I feel very strongly that I should go up, it is brighter, less damp, and I can escape through a window should the worst come to pass. This is the tactical choice, it is not the one I am making.



I will go down. I am searching for a secret, and those tend to be buried in the deepest possible places.

[[/div]]





[[/tab]]



[[tab Nursery]]



[[div class="addendum" style="float: var(--image-float); margin: 1rem; width: 60%;"]]

[[image nursery.png style="animation: blur-in 1s;"]]

[[/div]]

[[div class="genbox highlight" style="margin-left: var(--docHighlightMargin);"]]

I find myself at a nursery. This is not altogether unexpected. Large Foundation sites, which L13 certainly was, very commonly contain nurseries. Researchers live on site, have kids, stuff happens. The oddity comes from this particular nursery. It is profoundly old, decades older than the site. Older than the original opera house itself. The place stinks to high heaven, something is rotting but I cannot guess what. I cannot imagine why this place was created in its current state. It contains capacity for only 4 children, the average Foundation nursery should be able to hold over a hundred.



Stranger still is that 3 of the beds have severely decayed, but one hasn't. The sheets are ruffled and dust has not settled in. Someone has slept here recently.

[[/div]]



@@@@

@@@@

[[div class="genbox highlight"]]

I pried further into the used bed. Didn't find much at first, until I checked under the pillow. There was a human eye, severed violently. I am leaving this room, something in my gut finds it deeply uncomfortable.



**UPDATE:** Once I closed the door, I heard the brief wail of a baby come from within. I did not hear this when I first approached. It was quickly silenced. I could have sworn I heard a 'shush'. I think I made a good choice by taking off my shoes.

[[/div]]





[[/tab]]





[[tab Armory]]



[[div class="addendum" style="float: var(--image-float); margin: 1rem; width: 60%;"]]

[[image armory.png style="animation: blur-in 1s;"]]

[[/div]]

[[div class="genbox highlight" style="margin-left: var(--docHighlightMargin);"]]

I am in an armory. It is very standard, exactly as you'd expect. It's maybe the first thing I've seen that is as I'd expect. It is this prospect I find the most unsettling. It has all the standard munitions, though no records. I can't find any mission case files, nor any inkling of the men who used to use this room. In a place so otherwise untouched, it seems strange that the files specifically are what has been taken.



I am sorely tempted to use this opportunity to arm myself. I, of course, am armed with a standard Foundation handgun, though that is a small ordinance compared to what I find on these walls. I cannot tell if taking a gun would upset this place, or if it would simply be following the customs as I did in the mudroom. This is a dilemma, there is no right answer, but only in one answer do I get a gun, it hangs now from my belt.

[[/div]]



@@@@

@@@@

[[div class="genbox highlight"]]

In terms of oddities, there is one, the bullets. Almost all the heavy weapon ammo is gone (though mercifully not that of the high caliber pistol I selected), the casings remain, piled up in drawers, but the payloads are gone. It is like every bullet has been used.



Stranger still is what accompanies the casings. Crosses, Stars of David, and other assorted religious iconography, enormous amounts of it. It is like after the bullets ran out, they tried turning to these symbols as surrogates. It is possible that this explains the religious connotations of the sign outside, though I somewhat doubt it. My gut tells me that that sign warns of something I have not yet seen.

[[/div]]





[[/tab]]



